From 8c0e77099766f334b17fbb7270e7fff5c9cec246 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Helge Deller <deller@gmx.de>
Date: Mon, 13 Nov 2023 16:06:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/25] prctl: Temporarily disable prctl(PR_SET_MDWE) on parisc
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

systemd-254 tries to use prctl(PR_SET_MDWE) for systemd's
MemoryDenyWriteExecute functionality, but fails on PA-RISC/HPPA which
still needs executable stacks.

Temporarily disable prctl(PR_SET_MDWE) by returning -ENODEV on parisc
for now. Note that we can't return -EINVAL since systemd will then try
to use seccomp instead.

Reported-by: Sam James <sam@gentoo.org>
Signed-off-by: Helge Deller <deller@gmx.de>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/875y2jro9a.fsf@gentoo.org/
Link: https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/29775.
Cc: <stable@vger.kernel.org> # v6.3+
Signed-off-by: Michał Górny <mgorny@gentoo.org>
---
 kernel/sys.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/sys.c b/kernel/sys.c
index 47cb10a16b00..73b3b9e9bd79 100644
--- a/kernel/sys.c
+++ b/kernel/sys.c
@@ -2728,10 +2728,16 @@ SYSCALL_DEFINE5(prctl, int, option, unsigned long, arg2, unsigned long, arg3,
 		break;
 #endif
 	case PR_SET_MDWE:
-		error = prctl_set_mdwe(arg2, arg3, arg4, arg5);
+		if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PARISC))
+			error = -EINVAL;
+		else
+			error = prctl_set_mdwe(arg2, arg3, arg4, arg5);
 		break;
 	case PR_GET_MDWE:
-		error = prctl_get_mdwe(arg2, arg3, arg4, arg5);
+		if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PARISC))
+			error = -EINVAL;
+		else
+			error = prctl_get_mdwe(arg2, arg3, arg4, arg5);
 		break;
 	case PR_SET_VMA:
 		error = prctl_set_vma(arg2, arg3, arg4, arg5);
